# AI Agent Memory Architectures & Continuous Learning

**Status:** STABLE
**Created:** 2026-06-02
**Last Deepened:** 2026-06-02
**Interest Domain:** AI Agent Architecture & Local Inference
**Primary Sources:** 10/10 verified (2025-2026)
**Cross-links:** [adaptive-supervisor-architecture](adaptive-supervisor-architecture.md), [self-improving-agent-patterns](self-improving-agent-patterns.md), [llm-native-entity-resolution-scale-draft](llm-native-entity-resolution-scale-draft.md)

---

## Overview

How autonomous AI agents maintain state, retrieve knowledge, and learn continuously across sessions. The 2025-2026 literature converged on three architectural paradigms:
1. **Episodic + Semantic decomposition** — separate short-term working memory from long-term knowledge stores
2. **Graph-native memory** — temporal knowledge graphs replacing vector stores for structured recall
3. **Memory Operating Systems** — dedicated memory management layers abstracting storage, retrieval, and forgetting

---

## Key Architectural Paradigms (2025-2026)

### 1. Episodic + Semantic Memory Split

**arXiv 2512.13564** (Memory in the Age of AI Agents, 2025): Comprehensive survey identifying field fragmentation. Core finding: existing works differ substantially in motivations, implementations, and evaluation protocols. Proposes unified taxonomy across episodic, semantic, procedural, and meta-memory types.

**arXiv 2603.07670** (Memory for Autonomous LLM Agents, 2026): Introduces MemoryAgentBench grounding evaluation in cognitive science, probing four competencies: accurate retrieval, test-time learning, long-range understanding, and selective forgetting.

### 2. Graph-Native Memory

**arXiv 2602.05665** (Graph-based Agent Memory, 2026): Taxonomy of graph-based memory systems. Key insight: unstructured memory representations fail at reasoning essential for complex decision-making.

**arXiv 2601.03236** (MAGMA: Multi-Graph Agentic Memory, 2026): Multi-graph architecture combining semantic knowledge graphs with episodic event graphs. Includes predict-calibrate mechanism for episodic segmentation.

**Zep** (Temporal Knowledge Graph Architecture, 2025): Production memory layer service outperforming MemGPT on Deep Memory Retrieval benchmark.

### 3. Memory Operating Systems

**MemoryOS** (arXiv 2506.06326, 2025): Proposes dedicated Memory Operating System to overcome fixed context window limitations.

**AriGraph** (IJCAI 2025): Agent constructs and updates a memory graph integrating semantic and episodic memories while exploring environments.


---

## Benchmarks & Evaluation

### LoCoMo Benchmark (Mem0, ECAI 2025 — arXiv 2504.19413)
First head-to-head comparison of 10 memory approaches: literature baselines, open-source tools, RAG, full-context, OpenAI Memory, and Zep. Established baseline for selective memory.

### MemoryAgentBench (arXiv 2603.07670)
Cognitive-science-grounded evaluation probing four competencies: accurate retrieval, test-time learning, long-range understanding, and selective forgetting.

### LongMemEval
Enterprise-focused benchmark testing complex temporal reasoning tasks. Zep validated against this benchmark.

---

## Production Implementations (2025-2026)

| System | Approach | Status | Key Differentiator |
|--------|----------|--------|--------------------|
| **Zep** | Temporal KG | Production | Outperforms MemGPT on DMR; enterprise temporal reasoning |
| **Mem0** | Vector + Graph hybrid | Production/Research | LoCoMo benchmark baseline; ECAI 2025 paper |
| **MemGPT** | Functional memory | Production | Function-calling based memory management |
| **MemoryOS** | OS abstraction | Research | Comprehensive memory lifecycle management |
| **MAGMA** | Multi-graph | Research | Predict-calibrate episodic segmentation |

---

## Failure Modes & Open Challenges

| Failure Mode | Severity | Description | Status |
|-------------|----------|-------------|--------|
| **Context window exhaustion** | Critical | Long sessions exceed context budget; memory retrieval overhead compounds | Partial: MemoryOS, selective forgetting |
| **Temporal coherence loss** | High | Agents lose track of event ordering across sessions | Partial: Zep temporal KG |
| **Selective forgetting** | High | Agents retain irrelevant or harmful information | Research-stage: MemoryAgentBench probing |
| **Graph maintenance overhead** | Medium | Knowledge graph updates are computationally expensive at scale | Partial: MAGMA predict-calibrate |
| **Cross-domain transfer** | Medium | Memory from one domain interferes with another | Research-stage |


